DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_1 = Formula("10/((sin(x)))");
$fun_2 = Formula("1*x");
$fun_3 = Formula("x/5");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_3]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_3->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_3->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
